      "type": "note",
      "x": 760,
      "y": 40,
      "rotation": 0,
      "props": {
        "text": "A thermostat. The NTC {R1} and {R2} divide 12 V: as the NTC warms, its resistance falls and the voltage between them rises, until it turns transistor {K1} on through {R3}. That pulls in relay {K2}, whose changeover moves from heater {E1} to fan {M1}.\nA relay pulls in at a higher coil voltage than it lets go, so it switches a few degrees apart each way. {R4} catches the coil’s kick.",
        "color": "blue"
      },
      "broken": false
    },
    {
      "id": "c17",
      "ref": "N2",
      "usRef": "N2",
      "type": "note",
      "x": 760,
      "y": 260,
      "rotation": 0,
      "props": {
        "text": "Try: press Run and open the Thermal view. The heater warms the NTC, the relay clicks over and the fan cools it, then back again. Change {R2} to set the temperature (higher, cooler), raise the ambient, or turn the fan away.",
        "color": "amber"
      },
      "broken": false
    }
